## 1️⃣  Define the inference pipeline & its components  

| Component (logical) | Typical operations | Rough GPU/CPU split* |
|---------------------|--------------------|----------------------|
| **Pre‑processing** (tokenisation, OCR, text‑cleaning) | CPU‑only (text handling, regex, tokeniser) | 100 % CPU |
| **Embedding layer** (e.g., BERT/LegalBERT tokenizer + embedding lookup) | GPU‑accelerated matrix multiplies (if a transformer model is used) | ~90 % GPU, 10 % CPU (for tokenisation) |
| **Encoder / Transformer blocks** (e.g., 12‑layer BERT) | Heavy matrix‑multiply + attention – best on GPU | ~95 % GPU, 5 % CPU |
| **Task‑specific head** (classification, NER, similarity) | Small fully‑connected layers – can run on GPU or CPU | ~80 % GPU, 20 % CPU |
| **Post‑processing** (thresholding, formatting, DB write) | CPU‑only | 100 %",2595.7
